class.description:
[LanguageSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"language"[/code]: it stores the locale chosen by the player and related options, loads them when the game starts and applies them to [TranslationServer] and the root window. The settings resource is a [LanguageSettings]. The file is [code]user://settings/language.ini[/code] by default; as a single record it is never stored as CSV.
The domain is applied in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], after the project translations are loaded and before the main loop, the autoloads and the main scene exist, so the first text the player sees is already in the stored language. The layout direction and the auto-translate mode of the root window are pushed as soon as the root window exists, at the latest in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE], before the main scene is loaded.
The locale is chosen in this order: the command line argument [code]--language[/code] (or [code]-l[/code]), then [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/locale/test], then the stored locale, then the locale of the operating system. The first two are set as a session override (see [method SettingsServer.set_session_override]) when the game starts: they are applied but never saved, and a call to [method set_locale] replaces them.
An empty locale follows the operating system. A stored locale for which no translation is loaded (for example a language removed in a game update) is replaced by [method get_project_locale] when it is applied, with a verbose message only and no error; the stored value stays, so it is used again once the translation exists. If the project has no translations at all, the locale is set as it is.
A change of the locale or of pseudolocalization sends [constant MainLoop.NOTIFICATION_TRANSLATION_CHANGED], so auto-translated nodes update themselves. Texts that a script translated with [method Object.tr] and stored must be translated again.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	var language_list = $LanguageList
	language_list.add_item("System language")
	language_list.set_item_metadata(0, "")
	for locale in LanguageSettingsServer.get_available_locales():
		language_list.add_item(TranslationServer.get_locale_name(locale))
		language_list.set_item_metadata(language_list.item_count - 1, locale)
		if locale == LanguageSettingsServer.get_locale():
			language_list.select(language_list.item_count - 1)

func _on_language_list_item_selected(index):
	LanguageSettingsServer.set_locale($LanguageList.get_item_metadata(index))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    var languageList = GetNode<OptionButton>("LanguageList");
    languageList.AddItem("System language");
    languageList.SetItemMetadata(0, "");
    foreach (string locale in LanguageSettingsServer.GetAvailableLocales())
    {
        languageList.AddItem(TranslationServer.GetLocaleName(locale));
        languageList.SetItemMetadata(languageList.ItemCount - 1, locale);
        if (locale == LanguageSettingsServer.GetLocale())
        {
            languageList.Select(languageList.ItemCount - 1);
        }
    }
}

private void OnLanguageListItemSelected(long index)
{
    var languageList = GetNode<OptionButton>("LanguageList");
    LanguageSettingsServer.SetLocale(languageList.GetItemMetadata((int)index).AsString());
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]LanguageSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]LanguageSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] The Web export has no command line, so [code]--language[/code] has no effect there. The locale of the operating system is the browser language.
